<title>GERMANY: Fresenius Medical greenshoe exercised.</title>
<headline>Fresenius Medical greenshoe exercised.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dresdner Bank and CS First Boston as issuing coordinators said on Friday they had exercised the so-called greenshoe oversubscription share option in Fresenius Medical Care, the German dialysis group.</p>
<p>The greenshoe option of 400,000 preference shares at a nominal value of five marks each comes from an increase of the base capital of the company to 377 million marks, they said.</p>
<p>A maximum of 750,000 shares could have been exercised.</p>
<p>Last month the group issued five million new non-voting preference shares.</p>
<p>The coordinators said the shares had been sucessfully placed with national and international investors.</p>
<p>On the basis of the issuing price of 125 marks per share the new issue raised around 675 million marks, they said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
